      "text": "1. Let the unknown number be \\( x \\).\n2. According to the problem, \\( 20\\% \\) of \\( 10\\% \\) of \\( x \\) is equal to 12. We can express this relationship mathematically as:\n   \\[\n   0.20 \\times 0.10 \\times x = 12\n   \\]\n3. Simplify the left side of the equation:\n   \\[\n   0.02x = 12\n   \\]\n4. To find \\( x \\), divide both sides of the equation by 0.02:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{12}{0.02} = 600\n   \\]\n5. Now, we need to find \\( 10\\% \\) of \\( 20\\% \\) of \\( x \\). First, calculate \\( 20\\% \\) of \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   0.20 \\times 600 = 120\n   \\]\n6. Next, calculate \\( 10\\% \\) of \\( 120 \\):\n   \\[\n   0.10 \\times 120 = 12\n   \\]\n7. Therefore, \\( 10\\% \\) of \\( 20\\% \\) of the number is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{12}\n   \\]",
